+    WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not `effective_severity`, and the difference is the
+    GUARD rather than the arithmetic. `effective_severity` returns
+    `asserted * V` behind `_SEVERITY_SPEC["on"]` for the A4 door, where the
+    release is CONJUNCTIVE with `severity_is_proven`. The critical partition has
+    no such conjunct, so the V(None)=0.5 halving would act there unguarded: on
+    the archive, replacing the partition's severity with `asserted * V` flips
+    the real `_check_gamma_alt_convergence` on 11 of 67 runs, EVERY ONE
+    False -> True and EVERY ONE through the vacuous-curve branch (producer:
+    `scripts/which_direction_does_dropping_confidence_flip_the_gate_2026-11-04.py`).
+    That is a manufactured convergence, which releases defects. This function
+    therefore applies the ANNIHILATOR ONLY: V == 0 gives 0, and every other
+    value passes the asserted number through unchanged. Measured in the same
+    producer, under both A4 replay variants: 0 of 67 archived gate verdicts
+    move, Wilson [0.0000%, 5.4226%].
+
+    THE `status == "CONFIRMED"` CARVE-OUT IS MEASURED, NOT PRECAUTIONARY. One
+    archived entry carries `falsifier_verdict == "REFUTED"` while its status is
+    CONFIRMED (`arm1_harvest` C0048, asserted severity 0.8) -- 1 of 3,170
+    (producer: `scripts/is_a_refuted_falsifier_verdict_terminal_2026-11-04.py`).
+    CONFIRMED status is TOOL-ONLY in this registry: a model-requested CONFIRMED
+    is substituted to CORROBORATED and the substitution is recorded in
+    `refused_transitions`. So where the two disagree, zeroing on the stale
+    verdict field would drop a tool-CONFIRMED critical out of the count, and the
+    direction of that error is the expensive one -- the brief's own asymmetry,
